{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Industrial Grind Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: the heavy, distorted synth bass of industrial rock and metal, built to sit under (or double) down-tuned guitars: thick, saturated, a little snarl at the start of each note.\n\nHow it's built: two saws a few cents apart plus a sine an octave below for weight, mixed and pushed hard through Drive (with a touch of FOLD for the snarl), then the Ladder filter to tame the fizz. A filter envelope opens it a little on each note; the VCA's envelope holds while you hold the key. One voice, so you can play it legato like a bass guitar.\n\nPlay: low riffs, short notes, palm-mute style.\n\nTweak: DRIVE and FOLD; the filter's CUTOFF (darker sits under guitars, brighter cuts through); TUNE on the second oscillator for more or less width.",
